data.content:
## What Changed

.NET 10's `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgraded from **Microsoft.OpenApi v1.x → v2.x**, which has several breaking changes:

| Area | v1 (.NET 9) | v2 (.NET 10) |
|------|-------------|--------------|
| Example values | `OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc. from `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` | `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` |
| Nullable | `schema.Nullable = true/false` | `schema.Type` flags include/exclude `JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| References | `obj.Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ..., Id = ... }` | Dedicated reference types, e.g. `OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference` |
| Security requirements | `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` inherits `Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>` | Has a `Schemes` dictionary of `<OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference, IList<string>>` |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;          // replaces Microsoft.OpenApi.Any
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;  // for reference types

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // OpenApiString is gone; use JsonNode instead
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    // This still works as-is
    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    // Reference wrapper types replace OpenApiReference + ReferenceType
    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");

    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new()
        {
            Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference, IList<string>>
            {
                [oAuthScheme] = scopes
            }
        }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
            {
                // Nullable property is removed; clear the Null flag from Type instead
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
            }
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

### Summary of each fix

1. **`new OpenApiString("1.0")`** → `JsonValue.Create("1.0")` — the `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` namespace no longer exists; all example/default values are `JsonNode`.

2. **`OpenApiSecurityScheme { Reference = ... }`** → `new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2")` — inline `Reference` properties are gone; use dedicated reference types from `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References`.

3. **`{ [oAuthScheme] = scopes }`** → `Schemes = new Dictionary<...> { ... }` — `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` is no longer a dictionary itself; it exposes a `Schemes` property.

4. **`property.Value.Nullable = false`** → `property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null` — nullability is now a flag on the `Type` enum (`JsonSchemaType.Null`).
